CHAPTER.VERS:
Now the serpent was more subtle than any beast of the field which Yahweh God had made. And he said to the woman, has God really said, You

          {+}
         will not eat of any tree of the garden?

but of the fruit of the tree which is in the midst of the garden, God has said, You

          {+}
         will not eat of it, neither will you

          {+}
         touch it, or else you

          {+}
         will die.

And the serpent said to the woman, You

          {+}
         will not surely die:

for God knows that in the day you

          {+}
         eat of it, then your

          {+}
         eyes will be opened, and you

          {+}
         will be as God, knowing good and evil.
